# HTTP examples for the capstone. Start the platform first: capstone/up.sh (or: cd capstone && docker compose up --build)
# Everything goes through the gateway on port 8080.

### 3.1 A token for the demo customer (dev profile of the gateway)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "ayse", "password": "ayse-demo"}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 3.1 The catalog is public
GET http://localhost:8080/api/catalog/books

### 3.6 Search (run it twice: the second answer comes from the Redis cache)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/search?q=kafka

### 3.3 Place an order (the stock is reserved over gRPC)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"lines": [{"isbn": "9781492078005", "quantity": 2}]}

### 3.3 My orders
GET http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3.3 Not enough stock → 409 ProblemDetail
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"lines": [{"isbn": "9781492078005", "quantity": 50}]}

### 3.7 Without a token → 401 from the gateway
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"lines": [{"isbn": "9781492078005", "quantity": 1}]}

### 3.7 A token for the admin, then change a book (only ADMIN may)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "admin", "password": "admin-demo"}

> {% client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

###
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/catalog/books/9780132350884
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Clean Code", "authors": ["Robert C. Martin"], "description": "A handbook of agile software craftsmanship.",
 "price": 70.00, "stock": 12}
